@startuml
title From a token offer to a published white paper (Title II)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EAF4F4
  BorderColor #2F6F73
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #2F6F73
}
start
:Planned offer to the public or
admission to trading of a crypto-asset
other than an ART or EMT;
if (Free, protocol reward, live utility
token or limited network? (Art. 4(3))) then (yes)
  if (Listing announced? (Art. 4(4))) then (no)
    :Outside Title II;<<#B7DBDB>>
    stop
  endif
endif
if (< 150 persons per Member State,
≤ EUR 1 000 000 in 12 months,
or qualified investors only? (Art. 4(2))) then (yes)
  if (Listing announced? (Art. 4(4))) then (no)
    :No white paper;
    :Still a legal person,
    still Art. 14 conduct;<<#B7DBDB>>
    stop
  endif
endif
:Draw up the white paper (Art. 6, Annex I)
ten blocks, warnings, summary,
management-body statement;
:Notify the home competent authority
≥ 20 working days before publication
with the classification analysis (Art. 8);
:Authority forwards to host authorities
and to the ESMA register (Art. 8(6)–(7));
:Publish on the website before the
offer or admission starts (Art. 9);
:Marketing only after publication (Art. 7(2));
:Offer throughout the Union,
no further information requirements (Art. 11);<<#B7DBDB>>
repeat
  :Offer runs; retail buyers may withdraw
  within 14 days (Art. 13);
  if (Significant new factor or
  material mistake? (Art. 12)) then (yes)
    :Notify modified white paper
    ≥ 7 working days before publication;
    :Publish, time-stamp, keep old versions 10 years;
  endif
repeat while (Token still offered or listed?) is (yes)
->no;
stop
@enduml
